ues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n-Reproducible in 4.6.2 stable, 4.6.2 RC2 (no other 4.6.2 versions tested)\n-Not reproducible 4.6.1, 4.6.0.\n\n\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11, RTX 3090, Godot 4.6.2 stable\n\n### Issue description\n\nAfter updating from 4.6.1 stable to 4.6.2 the option \"Use custom timeline\" in blendtree's Animation nodes seems to crop the animation even if \"Stretch time line\" is selected. \n\nNot all animation channels types seem to be affected by this bug.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI'm including a simple project that exposed the bug, a simple 1 second animation loop calls a method that prints a string at 0.75 seconds. The animation is played through an animation node in a Blendtree with a custom timeline of length 0.50 and the option \"Stretch Time Scale\" activated.\n\nThe expected behavior, and the one happening in older version, is that the string will be printed on the console at 0.75s/2 = 0.375s, instead the string is never printed and any method call past the 0.5 mark will be ignored.\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[b-tree-bug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26426218/b-tree-bug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs